=== Prompt ===
Who is Che Guevara?

=== Response ===
Che Guevara was a highly influential and iconic Argentine Marxist revolutionary, physician, author, guerrilla leader, diplomat, and key figure in the Cuban Revolution. His full name was Ernesto Guevara de la Serna, but he was commonly known as Che Guevara.

Born on June 14, 1928, in Rosario, Argentina, Che Guevara grew up in a middle-class family. He studied medicine at the University of Buenos Aires, but his true passion was politics. In 1953, he traveled to Peru, then to Bolivia, and eventually to Guatemala, where he became involved in the anti-imperialist and anti-capitalist movements.

In 1955, Che Guevara traveled to Mexico, where he met Fidel Castro, a Cuban revolutionary leader. The two men quickly became close friends and began to plan a revolution in Cuba. In 1956, Che Guevara joined Fidel Castro's group of rebels, known as the 26th of July Movement, which aimed to overthrow the authoritarian government of Fulgencio Batista in Cuba.

On November 26, 1956, Che Guevara and a group of about 80 rebels sailed from Mexico to Cuba on the yacht Granma. The group was ambushed by Batista's forces, but they managed to survive and eventually regroup. Over the next two years, Che Guevara and Castro's forces fought a guerrilla war against the Batista regime, using tactics such as ambushes, sabotage, and raids.

On January 1, 1959, the Cuban Revolution succeeded, and Fidel Castro's forces overthrew the Batista government. Che Guevara became a key figure in the new government, serving as Minister of Industry, President of the National Bank, and Minister of the Interior. He also played a crucial role in the establishment of Cuba's socialist economy and the country's relations with the Soviet Union.

However, Che Guevara's time in Cuba was marked by controversy. He was known for his radical views, his advocacy of violence, and his criticism of the Soviet Union's policies. He also became increasingly isolated from Fidel Castro and the Cuban leadership.

